cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use OpenDubs in academic work, please cite it as below."
title: "OpenDubs: a low-cost, open-source mobile robot"
abstract: >-
  OpenDubs is a low-cost, low-fabrication, open-source mobile robot platform built from mostly
  off-the-shelf parts (an NVIDIA Jetson AGX Thor, an M5Stack StamPLC safety controller, goBILDA
  and REV structure, a mecanum drive, two OpenArm arms and a tablet head) with open firmware,
  software and hardware designs, so that others can replicate it.
type: software
authors:
  # TODO: the copyright holder and the author list wait on legal advice (individual contributors
  # or the University of Washington). Until then the project is cited as one collective author.
  - name: "The OpenDubs Authors"
repository-code: "https://github.com/UW-Allen-School-Robotics/opendubs"
url: "https://uw-allen-school-robotics.github.io/opendubs/"
license:
